1. Ownership

DefenderTray — including its source code, the PowerShell scripts of every
version stored in this repository, its graphical interface, the embedded
templates (MSI, Docker, PWA, HTML panels), icons, texts, documentation
(README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, SECURITY.md, and this document), and the
"DefenderTray" name and mark — (the "Software") is owned by yhquintero
(the "Owner") and is protected by applicable intellectual property
legislation and international treaties.

2. Visible code, not open source

The repository being public and the code being readable does not make the
Software free or open source. No license or right is granted, whether
express or implied, beyond those expressly stated in this document.

3. Permitted uses without authorization

No authorization from the Owner is required in order to:

  a) view, study, and download the source code;

  b) fork the repository within GitHub, to the extent permitted by
     GitHub's Terms of Service, solely to read the code or to propose
     contributions to the original repository through pull requests;

  c) use the Software on machines you own or are explicitly authorised to
     administer, for personal, educational, laboratory, or diagnostic
     purposes, non-commercially, and without distributing copies to third
     parties;

  d) run the Software inside your own organisation's internal working
     environment, by its own staff and under its own responsibility,
     provided the Software is not redistributed or offered to third
     parties;

  e) modify the code for the private use contemplated above, without
     distributing the resulting work;

  f) report bugs or vulnerabilities as described in SECURITY.md.

4. Uses requiring prior written authorization

Unless the Owner gives prior written authorization, the following are
prohibited:

  a) copying, reproducing, modifying, translating, adapting, or creating
     derivative works of the Software, in whole or in part, for purposes
     other than those permitted by clause 3;

  b) distributing, publishing, sublicensing, selling, renting, lending,
     giving away, packaging, embedding in system images or third-party
     installers, or otherwise making the Software or its derivatives
     available to the public, including mirror repositories, forums,
     download portals, cloud hosting, and SaaS offerings;

  c) using the Software, its derivatives, or its interfaces as a component
     of your own product or service, whether commercial or free;

  d) offering the Software, its features, or its maintenance as a service
     to third parties (consulting, managed deployments, remote support);

  e) removing, hiding, or altering copyright, trademark, or license
     notices, the script headers, or authorship information;

  f) using the "DefenderTray" name or logo, or the Owner's names, to
     identify other products or services, or to suggest affiliation,
     endorsement, or sponsorship;

  g) presenting the Software or a modified version as your own.

5. Responsible use and limits

The Software controls Microsoft Windows security protections (Microsoft
Defender Antivirus, SmartScreen, tamper protection, related services and
Group Policy settings). By using it, you acknowledge that:

  a) you will use it only on machines you own or are explicitly authorised
     to administer, and with the consent of your organisation's security
     owner where internal rules require it;

  b) using it, or variants of it, to circumvent, weaken, disable, or
     disable-by-persistence the security controls of machines you do not
     own, to facilitate unauthorised access to a system, to deploy or run
     malware, or to conceal malicious activity, is prohibited;

  c) obfuscating, renaming, splitting, recompiling, or otherwise
     modifying the Software in order to evade detection by security
     products is prohibited;

  d) the Owner authorises no use of the Software that constitutes
     unlawful access to systems, interference with data, or breach of
     applicable computer-security rules;

  e) disabling protections may leave a machine exposed, breach your
     organisation's regulatory or contractual requirements, invalidate
     insurance or certifications, and require a reboot to return the
     system to a consistent state: verifying the state after each use is
     your responsibility.

6. Contributions

By submitting a contribution (pull request, patch, issue, comment,
documentation fix, or suggestion), you represent that you are its author or
have the right to submit it, and you grant the Owner a worldwide,
perpetual, irrevocable, royalty-free, non-exclusive, and transferable
license to use, reproduce, modify, sublicense, and distribute that
contribution as part of the Software or of other products, with no
obligation to compensate you.

Contributors further warrant that their contribution contains no third
party secrets, personal data about other people, credentials, or code
under licenses incompatible with this document, and that it is not
intended to circumvent the security controls of machines belonging to
others.

Contributing grants you no right to use the Software beyond those in
clause 3.

7. Third-party components, services, and data

The Software does not embed compiled third-party libraries, but it may
download, install, or connect to third-party components and services (for
example the SQLite access provider, WiX Toolset, Microsoft PowerShell
modules, Active Directory, Microsoft Excel, OneDrive, Telegram,
Firebase/Google, SMTP relays, and webhook receivers). Those components and
services are governed by their own licenses, terms, and privacy policies,
which prevail over this document with respect to those components. The
Software does not modify or broaden any third-party license, and the Owner
is not the provider of those services.

The files, logs, registry backups, screenshots, and databases the
Software generates on your machine are yours; the Owner does not collect
or store them.

